<div class="app">
  <header>
    <div class="team blue">
      <div class="score" id="blue-score">0</div>
      <div><div class="rps"><div class="rp" id="blue-rows" data-icon="rows" title="Rows of three goals owned: 10 points each"></div><div class="rp" id="blue-endzone" data-icon="endzone" title="All three robots in the end zone at the end: 10 points"></div></div><div class="meta" id="blue-pieces"></div><div class="meta" id="blue-extra"></div></div>
    </div>
    <div class="center"><div id="clock">∞</div><div id="phase">Free play</div><div class="meta" id="sub"></div></div>
    <div class="team red">
      <div><div class="rps"><div class="rp" id="red-rows" data-icon="rows" title="Rows of three goals owned: 10 points each"></div><div class="rp" id="red-endzone" data-icon="endzone" title="All three robots in the end zone at the end: 10 points"></div></div><div class="meta" id="red-pieces"></div><div class="meta" id="red-extra"></div></div>
      <div class="score" id="red-score">0</div>
    </div>
  </header>
  <main><canvas id="field" aria-label="Field"></canvas>
  </main>
  <aside>
    <div class="buttons">
      <button id="setup">Pre-match setup</button>
      <button class="primary" id="go">Start match</button>
      <button id="stop">Stop match</button>
      <button id="free">Free play</button>
      <button id="sound" aria-pressed="true">Sound on</button>
    </div>
    <div class="help">Pre-match setup resets the field and stops the clock. Drag robots into their end zone (scroll over a robot to turn it): the middle spot may reach out to the middle wall goal. Start match runs 0:15 of autonomous, a short pause while the bonus tetras go on, then 2:00 of driver control. Free play has no clock.</div>
    <div id="results"></div>
    <h2>Game mode <span class="mode-chip" id="mode-chip"></span></h2>
    <div id="mode"></div>
    <h2>Robots</h2>
    <div id="robots"></div>
    <button id="add">Add robot</button>
    <div class="meta" id="pads"></div>
    <h2>How it plays</h2>
    <div class="help">
      Hover or click the <b>?</b> in the bottom-left corner of the field for every key and button.
      <b>Scoring</b> (counted at the end): a tetra <b>contained</b> in a goal's base is 1 point and one <b>stacked</b> on a goal's top is 3, for the alliance of its color. Whoever stacked last on a goal owns it (with nothing stacked, the alliance with more contained tetras does). Each row of three goals one alliance owns, tic-tac-toe style, is 10. All three robots in their end zone at the end is 10 more.
      <b>The arm</b>: every robot is modeled on 254's Kara (27 x 37 in frame). The gripper is on the end of an arm on the robot's centerline: turn the robot to aim it, raise it above the goal's top (the gauge beside the robot shows the arm's height against the goal in front), reach out over the apex, wait for the tetra to stop swinging and lower it until it seats, then open the gripper. Not lined up and it sits crooked and falls off. The double-jointed arm reaches every goal, the 7 ft center goal included; the lift stacker reaches the wall and side goals; the goal filler only drops tetras inside goals and pulls the other alliance's out.
      <b>Loading</b>: drive into one of your two automated loading zones (bottom rail) and take the tetra off the Tetra Loading Station; the attendant puts another on after you leave. Or stop in one of your manual loading zones (top rail) with the arm low and the gripper open: your human player steps off the pad and loads you, and your robot is disabled until they are back (G08). Leave a zone before you can load there again (G17).
      <b>Autonomous</b>: robots run their programs; nobody drives. A vision tetra stacked in autonomous earns bonus tetras on your corner goals. A tetra hangs in each corner goal until a robot knocks it down in autonomous.
      <b>Classic</b> mode is tank drive, no presets, no assists: the arm coasts past where you let go and a loaded arm sags slowly. <b>Normal</b> mode adds swerve, arm presets and gentle hold-to-stack, hold-to-contain and hold-to-pick-up assists for the spot you are aiming at within about 3 ft.
      Each robot's tier (S best to D worst) sets its drive speed, arm speed, how much the arm coasts and the tetra swings, gripper time and, in Normal mode, how often an assisted placement fails.
    </div>
  </aside>
</div>
